+## Findings
+- The duplicate-creation regression test exercises two concurrent runCli calls in one process, so it does not prove the intended cross-process CLI serialization behavior.
+
+## Evidence
+- .agentplane/tasks/202608061646-30TKV4/quality/objects/sha256/3a49c50099238097e8b103032d050c22a335492decec015c807fb273c428f729.patch
+- .agentplane/tasks/202608061646-30TKV4/README.md
+
+## Missing Tests
+- Spawn two independent task create CLI processes against the same repository and outcome, synchronize their start, and assert exactly one task is persisted while the other exits with the duplicate-validation result; also assert the persisted execution_route remains frozen and consistent.
+
+## Hidden Assumptions
+- withTaskReadmeTransaction provides correct mutual exclusion across independent operating-system processes, not only concurrent calls within one JavaScript runtime.
+
+## Residual Risks
+- Add deterministic cross-process duplicate-creation coverage for the filesystem transaction, then rerun the declared verification contract and record the result against the same implementation behavior.
